<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  A measurement target that answers instantly and then says nothing.

  Point a TeXML Application's Voice URL at this file and assign a number to it.
  Calls to that number are answered the moment TeXML is fetched, with no server
  to run and no tunnel to keep alive, which is what makes repeated unattended
  measurement possible. Pause holds the line long enough for the caller to take
  its readings and hang up first.

  Serve it from a CDN, not from raw.githubusercontent.com. Telnyx fetches this
  file on every single call, and under real load raw GitHub stops answering, so
  calls ring unanswered with nothing in any log to explain it. Twenty-five
  consecutive calls failed that way before the cause was clear. jsDelivr mirrors
  the same file, returns application/xml rather than text/plain, and held for
  every call:

    https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/<owner>/<repo>@main/docs/texml/answer.xml

  Used by the anchorsite comparison. Reusable by anyone who wants a number that
  picks up without a human.
-->
<Response>
  <Pause length="20"/>
</Response>
